<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.drivestudio.shared</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		CarPlay entitlement — gated behind Apple approval.
		Apply at https://developer.apple.com/contact/carplay/ — choose ONE of:
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-driving-task (broadest; recommended for Drive Studio)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-audio         (audio apps)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-maps          (navigation)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-messaging     (messaging)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-voip          (VoIP)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-fuel          (EV / fuel)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-parking       (parking)
		  - com.apple.developer.carplay-food-ordering (food)

		Until Apple grants the entitlement, keep this commented out — adding
		it without approval will fail provisioning. The widget still appears
		in the iPhone widget gallery without it, and the CarPlay scene
		registration in Info.plist is harmless (iOS just won't activate the
		CarPlay Dashboard widget list for unentitled apps).

		Once approved, uncomment the matching entitlement block below.
	-->
	<!--
	<key>com.apple.developer.carplay-driving-task</key>
	<true/>
	-->
</dict>
</plist>